title: Cue Playbook II: Duets and Trios
id: cue-pairs
tab: 27 · Cue Playbook II: Duets and Trios
about: 27 · Cue sets the tests: Gruff and Chip sing low and high at once, Neon and Tabby call and answer, and Watt, Clank and Zap come in one after another
lead: scribe
key: D
bpm: 108
beat: B . t K | . t B . | t B . K | . B t . (swing .1)
backing:
bass: none
finale: "Three" on 7

[duet, high and low]
# Two lines at once: Gruff below, Chip an octave and more above, moving in parallel.
"First a duet high and low" = 0/.5 2/.5 4 4 5 4 2/3 | I 4, V 4 ; do nod
gruff: "I sing low beneath the floor" = 0 -1 -3 -1 0 2 0/2 | I 4, IV 4
  + chip: "I sing high above the door" = 7 6 4 6 7 9 7/2
gruff: "Low and high we meet halfway" = 0 2 4 2 0 -1 0/2 | IV 4, I 4
  + chip: "High and low we meet halfway" = 7 5 4 5 7 8 7/2

[duet, call and answer]
"Now a duet call and reply" = 0/.5 2/.5 4 4/.5 5/.5 4 2 0/3 | I 4, V 4 ; do tilt
vee: "Is it twice" = 4 5 7/2 | I 4
tabby: "Yes it's twice" = 7 5 4/2 | V 4
vee: "Is it bright" = 4 5 7/2 | IV 4
tabby: "Shining bright" = 7 5 4/2 | I 4 ; do nod

[trio, one after another]
# Watt starts, Clank joins two beats in, Zap four beats in.
"Now a trio three in a row" = 0/.5 2/.5 4 4/.5 5/.5 4 2 0/3 | I 4, V 4 ; do nod
pip: "Plug it in and turn it on" = 0 2 4 5 4 2 0/2 | I 4, V 4
  + clank @2: "Turn it on and wait" = 0 2 4 2 0/2
  + zap @4: "Click it on" = 7 5 4/2
pip: "Three of us all humming now" = 4 5 4 2 4 2 0/2 | IV 4, I 4 ; do gasp
  + clank @2: "Humming now" = 0 -1 0/4
  + zap @4: "Click click click" = 7 7 7/2
